-blocked"},"clock":{"displayValue":"2:07"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"27"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4233880","displayName":"Alexandre Texier","shortName":"A. Texier"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"5080180","displayName":"Reid Schaefer","shortName":"R. Schaefer"},"type":"defender"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1831","fullName":"Bell Centre","address":{"city":"Montreal","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1831.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":20962,"officials":[{"fullName":"Cody Beach","displayName":"Cody Beach","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kendrick Nicholson","displayName":"Kendrick Nicholson","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Caleb Apperson","displayName":"Caleb Apperson","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jonathan Deschamps","displayName":"Jonathan Deschamps","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Ryan O'Reilly scores go-ahead goal as Predators rally for 5-2 win over Canadiens","description":"— Ryan O’Reilly scored the go-ahead goal with 3:16 remaining, and the Nashville Predators rallied from a 2-0 deficit to beat the Montreal Canadiens 5-2 on Thursday night.","story":"MONTREAL -- — Ryan O’Reilly scored the go-ahead goal with 3:16 remaining, and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nsh/nashville-predators\">Nashville Predators</a> rallied from a 2-0 deficit to beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/mtl/montreal-canadiens\">Montreal Canadiens</a> 5-2 on Thursday night.\n\n\r\n              The veteran redirected a point shot from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5436/roman-josi\">Roman Josi</a> on the power play, 59 seconds after Canadiens defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2976851/mike-matheson\">Mike Matheson</a> tripped <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5037/steven-stamkos\">Steven Stamkos</a> in the neutral zone.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4894222/adam-edstrom\">Adam Edstrom</a> added a pair of empty-net goals for Nashville, which was outshot 34-18.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3069394/alexander-kerfoot\">Alexander Kerfoot</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149189/matthew-wood\">Matthew Wood</a> also scored for the Predators, while <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042109/juuse-saros\">Juuse Saros</a> made 32 saves. Stamkos had two assists.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233594/nick-suzuki\">Nick Suzuki</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565237/alex-newhook\">Alex Newhook</a> scored for Montreal, which extended its winless streak to three games. Jacob Fowler stopped 15 shots in his first start of the season.\n\n\r\n              Montreal ended a streak of five straight wins against Nashville dating to March 5, 2024.\n\n\r\n              After a scoreless first period, Suzuki opened the scoring for Montreal 3:12 into the second during four-on-four play. He collected a loose puck amid a scramble in front of the net and slid a backhander between Saros’ legs for his third goal of the season.\n\n\r\n              Newhook doubled Montreal’s lead at 8:50, finishing off Josh Anderson’s feed after minutes of sustained pressure in Nashville’s zone.\n\n\r\n              Kerfoot scored with 4:54 remaining in the period, redirecting Adam Wilsby’s point shot past Fowler on the glove side.\n\n\r\n              Wood tied the game on the power play with 32 seconds left in the period.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Predators: At Ottawa on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              Canadiens: Host Detroit on Saturday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-09T02:15:33Z"}}